374 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H1
/P 163 0 R
/T (8.3 Race Condition Prevention  The OpenMP update function avoids race conditions through thread-local accumulation. Each thread maintains private localSum and localCount arrays during the parallel for loop. Only the brief merge step is protected by #pragma omp critical, minimizing lock contention and maximizing throughput. )
/E (8.3 Race Condition Prevention  The OpenMP update function avoids race conditions through thread-local accumulation. Each thread maintains private localSum and localCount arrays during the parallel for loop. Only the brief merge step is protected by #pragma omp critical, minimizing lock contention and maximizing throughput. )
/Pg 18 0 R
/K [7]
>>
endobj
375 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H1
/P 163 0 R
/T (8.2 Why CPU + OpenMP for Update?  The centroid update is a reduction operation: summing coordinates across potentially thousands of points per cluster. Reductions have data dependencies and are less efficient on GPU without specialized techniques \(like atomics or parallel reduction trees\). OpenMP's thread-private arrays with a final critical-section merge is a simpler, equally effective approach for moderate-size datasets. )
/E (8.2 Why CPU + OpenMP for Update?  The centroid update is a reduction operation: summing coordinates across potentially thousands of points per cluster. Reductions have data dependencies and are less efficient on GPU without specialized techniques \(like atomics or parallel reduction trees\). OpenMP's thread-private arrays with a final critical-section merge is a simpler, equally effective approach for moderate-size datasets. )
/Pg 18 0 R
/K [8]
>>
endobj
