1047 0 obj
<<
/Title (8.2 Why CPU + OpenMP for Update?  The centroid update is a reduction operation: summing coordinates across potentially thousands of points per cluster. Reductions have data dependencies and are less efficient on GPU without specialized techniques \(like atomics or parallel reduction trees\). OpenMP's thread-private arrays with a final critical-section merge is a simpler, equally effective approach for moderate-size datasets.)
/Dest [18 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 7 0 R
/Prev 1052 0 R
/Next 1041 0 R
>>
endobj
